  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(f(x)=3x+2\\) for all real \\(x,\\) then the statement:\n\n“\\(|f(x)+4|\\lt a\\) whenever \\(|x+2|\\lt b\\) and \\(a\\gt0\\) and \\(b\\gt0\\)”\n\nis true when",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(b\\le \\frac{a}{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(b\\gt \\frac{a}{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(a\\le \\frac{b}{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(a\\gt \\frac{b}{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "The statement is never true."
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1974-p27.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\[ |f(x)+4|=|3x+6|=3|x+2|. \\] If \\(|x+2|\\lt b\\) and \\(b\\le \\frac{a}{3},\\) then \\(3|x+2|\\lt3b\\le a,\\) as required. If \\(b\\gt \\frac{a}{3},\\) one can choose \\(|x+2|\\) strictly between \\(\\frac{a}{3}\\) and \\(b,\\) so the statement fails. Thus the exact condition is \\(b\\le \\frac{a}{3}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(f(x)+4\\) in terms of \\(x+2\\)",
        "The condition becomes \\(3|x+2|\\lt a\\) whenever \\(|x+2|\\lt b\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
